% ============================================================
% Task 1: Deductive Chain (3-step syllogism)
% Tests whether confidence propagates correctly through a
% sequence of inheritance statements under resource pressure.
%
% Inference mode: Deduction (NAL-1)
% Ground truth target: <A --> C> with high f, c ~ f*c1*c2*c3
% ============================================================

% Step 1: A is a kind of B
<A --> B>. %{1.00 0.90}

% Step 2: B is a kind of C
<B --> C>. %{1.00 0.90}

% Step 3: C is a kind of D
<C --> D>. %{1.00 0.90}

% Query: What is the relationship between A and D?
<A --> D>?

% Expected: NARS should derive <A --> D> via:
%   A-->B + B-->C => A-->C (deduction)
%   A-->C + C-->D => A-->D (deduction)
% Ground-truth truth value: f*=1.0, c* ~ 0.9^3 / (1 + 0.9^3*(1/k-1)) ~ 0.73
